{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytSwapTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SytSwapTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytContentTuple"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.syt_swapStep_connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.syt_swapStep_connected","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytSwapTransport.lean#L129-L142","doc":"**Connectivity in the `SchurWeyl` API.**  Any two standard tableaux of one shape are joined by\na chain of admissible `swapTableau` steps — `syt_adjacentSwap_connected` carried across the bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.swapStep_of_adjacentSwapStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.swapStep_of_adjacentSwapStep","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytSwapTransport.lean#L78-L127","doc":"**The transport.**  An `AdjacentSwapStep` between the `BraidKnot` images is a `swapTableau`\nstep here.  The proof never touches `swapCellsSYT`: `AdjacentSwapStep` constrains only content\nvectors, `swapTableau` has the matching content profile, and separation\n(`syt_eq_of_cellContent_eq`) does the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.braidKnot_cellContent_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.braidKnot_cellContent_eq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytSwapTransport.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The two `cellContent`s — `QOU.SchurWeyl`'s and `QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy`'s — are distinct\ndeclarations with the same body `c.2 − c.1`, so they agree definitionally.  Named so the transport\nbelow never silently relies on that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SwapStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SwapStep","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytSwapTransport.lean#L66-L70","doc":"**One admissible swap step**, in the `SchurWeyl` API: `T'` is `T` with the labels `k` and\n`k+1` exchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.swapAdmissible_of_sq_axialDist_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.swapAdmissible_of_sq_axialDist_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytSwapTransport.lean#L38-L64","doc":"**`d² ≠ 1` is admissibility.**  Sharing a row forces axial distance `1`, sharing a column\nforces `−1`; so a gap that is neither is a genuine `2 × 2` swap. ","signatureChunk":0}]}